  "description": "NEMXIQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H82 Cu2 Dy4 N6 O24,C1 H4 O1,C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.348-3.908 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.15-113.35°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C98H84Cl2Cu2Dy4N6O25.",
